{
  "beruf": "buero",
  "title": "Office and admin",
  "level": "A2–B1",
  "reviewed": false,
  "_note": "italian-for-work run, 2026-11-15: written by hand for Italy, not yet read by a human or a second reader. translations.en = English meaning; deHint = German translation. Working conditions are general orientation only; facts marked 'to verify' in the run report.",
  "intro": "Office work in Italy means a lot of paperwork and a lot of polite phone calls: pratiche, protocollo, PEC, fatture and appointments. This deck has the office and its equipment, daily tasks, meetings and deadlines, data protection and filing, and what you say to clients and colleagues. With clients use Lei and titles (dottor, dottoressa, ingegnere, avvocato); with colleagues many offices use tu quickly, but let the other person offer it first.",
  "introEasy": "Do you work in an office in Italy? Learn the words for your work here.",
  "jobs": [
    "Impiegato/a amministrativo/a",
    "Segretario/a",
    "Addetto/a alla segreteria",
    "Receptionist",
    "Addetto/a al servizio clienti",
    "Addetto/a alla contabilità"
  ],
  "tipps": [
    "On the phone, say the company and your name: «Studio Rossi, buongiorno, sono Sara Bianchi.» «Pronto» is what you say when you pick up a private phone, and you also hear it in small offices. When you call, start with «Pronto, parlo con la signora Rossi?»",
    "Useful phone steps: «Le passo l'ufficio acquisti.», «Resti in linea, per favore.», «Può richiamare più tardi?», «Vuole lasciare un messaggio?»",
    "In emails, «Gentile dottoressa Bianchi,» is formal and «Ciao Anna,» is fine with colleagues. Close with «Cordiali saluti» (formal) or «A presto» (friendly). Italian greetings in emails are followed by a comma, not a colon.",
    "A PEC (posta elettronica certificata) is an email with legal value, like a registered letter. Companies and professionals must have one. Ask your colleagues before sending anything important by normal email.",
    "Do not leave personal data on your desk or send it by email without need. If you are unsure, ask: «Questo documento si può inviare per e-mail?»",
    "Contract, ferie, permessi, straordinario, malattia and the tredicesima depend on your contract and the CCNL of your sector. Ask the employer, a union (sindacato/patronato) or the Ispettorato del lavoro. This is general orientation, not legal advice."
  ],
